{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (81.82%) to hepcidin TH1-5 C: 36%, G=R: 14%. Chemical modification: N-terminal acetylation and C-terminal amidation. Activity: Active against Gram+ S. agalactiae LFY-5 (MIC 16 uM), S. aureus ATCC6538 (MIC 8 uM), Gram- E. piscicida (MIC 32 uM), V. harveyi QT520 (MIC 16 uM), V. alginolyticus HN08155 (MIC 64 uM), and E.coli ATCC8739 (MIC 128 uM). Structure: predicted to be beta-sheet. MOA:bacteria: depolarized and permeated bacterial membranes of S. agalactiae, S. aureus, E. piscicida, and V. harveyi. Updated 7/2025", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "37298202", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Int J Mol Sci. 2023 May 25;24(11):9251. doi: 10.3390/ijms24119251. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04732", "source_id": "AP04732", "source_numeric_id": "04732", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04732", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Antibacterial Activity and Mechanisms of TroHepc2-22, a Derived Peptide of Hepcidin2 from Golden Pompano (Trachinotus ovatus).", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
